WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.771 size:78% position:39% line:0%
Here we are in Edinburgh.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.305 size:75% position:38% line:0%
That's in Scotland, Dan.

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:07.640 align:start size:75% position:25% line:0%
- Well, thanks.
- Yeah.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.409 align:start size:66% position:34% line:0%
We're at the "FloWave
Research Facility"

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.676 align:start size:53% position:47%
at the University
of Edinburgh 

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:11.778 align:start size:75% position:25%
in this giant wave pool.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.646 align:start size:81% position:19%
It's about 82 feet across,

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.281 align:start size:53% position:47%
and it's got 168
individual little

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:16.682 align:start size:63% position:38%
wave pusher paddles.

00:00:16.715 --> 00:00:18.484
Gav:<i> It's capable
 of creating hundreds</i>

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:20.119
<i> of different types
 of waves found in nature,</i>

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:22.188
<i> for various testing purposes.</i>

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:24.323
<i> But with the simultaneous
 activation</i>

00:00:24.356 --> 00:00:26.159
<i> of all of the pushers,
 you can create</i>

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.560
<i> one giant spike wave
 right in the middle,</i>

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.796 align:start position:0%
and that's what
we're gonna get in slow-mo.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:75% position:25%
So we're here
for the fun, silly wave?

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.433 align:start size:88% position:13%
- That's correct, yeah.
- Okay, right.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.617 line:0%
Dan:<i> We've waited 
 for the water to settle,</i>

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.852 line:0%
<i> 'cause apparently
 that's the best</i>

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.787 line:0%
<i> to get the optimum large spike</i>

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.089 line:0%
<i> because any sort of
 disturbance in the water</i>

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.356
<i>dissipates the energy slightly.</i>

00:00:57.389 --> 00:00:59.192 align:start size:66% position:34%
So really focusing it
to the middle.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.494 align:start position:0%
Got the Phantom set
to 1,000 frames a second,

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.429 align:start position:0%
and we've also got
some very bright lights

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:06.132 align:start position:0%
concentrated on
the middle of the pool,

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.101 align:start position:0%
cause that's where
the spike wave is gonna be.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.335 align:start position:0%
I think we're ready.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.471
- I think so.
- Let's do it.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:16.242
Dan: Oh, you can see
the movement. Oh.

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:18.544 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Building up.
- It's weird to just
  have perfect ripples.

00:01:18.577 --> 00:01:20.546 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Building up.
- Oh, look at that.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:23.083
- Here we go.
- Here it is.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:31.157
- Whoa. Whoa!
- Flippin' A.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
- That was a really good one.
- That was really good.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.761 align:start size:75% position:25%
I liked how clear it was
in the middle.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:41.868
Gav:
<i> That is so weird looking.</i>

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.871
 Dan:<i> The grid on the floor,
 it makes it look really...</i>

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Gav:<i> It looks like--
 it looks like a wormhole. </i>
-<i> ...computer generated.</i>

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:48.574
Gav:<i> It looks like
 someone's just pulling</i>

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:50.743 align:start size:78% position:22%
 -<i> on space time.
 -</i> Dan:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:53.579
<i> Whoa.
 That's satisfyingly clear.</i>

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:57.183
Gav:<i> That is crazy.</i>

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.252 align:start position:0%
It looks like--
you know when you drop

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.887 size:84% position:42%
one single droplet in water

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.255 align:start position:0%
and it just goes...
( imitates drop )

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.590 align:start position:0%
It looks like that
on a massive scale.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.593
 Gav:<i> Look at what it did to
 the reflection on the wall.</i>

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.328 align:start size:97% position:3%
-<i> It focused.</i>
-<i> That's the light bouncing.</i>

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:10.663
Gav:<i> It was, like,
 briefly a magnifying glass</i>

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:13.266
<i> on that part of the wall.</i>

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Dan:<i> That's a weird look
 as well, isn't it? </i>
-<i> All falling back.</i>

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.772
Gav:<i> All right,
 look how much that sank down.</i>

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:22.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Gav:<i> That's really cool. </i>
- Dan:<i> Ahh.</i>

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:26.146
<i> ( both imitating splash )</i>

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:29.782 size:84% position:42%
I'm ready for the skadoosh.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:32.485
- Here we go.
- ( gasps )

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:38.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
- ( imitating splash )
- Oh!

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-<i> ( Dan laughs ) </i>
- Gav:<i> Absolutely colossal.</i>

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.672 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Gav:<i> Yeah, look at that.
 Traveling up the column. </i>
- Dan:<i> Oh, wow.</i>

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.642
<i> You matched the speed
 pretty well there.</i>

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:57.643
 Gav:<i> I caught up
 with it, yeah.</i>

00:02:57.676 --> 00:02:58.845
Dan:<i> That's solid.</i>

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.482 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Gav:<i> Oh, right in the roof. </i>
- Dan:<i> Good effort.</i>

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:05.818 align:start size:97% position:3%
-<i> At that point, it's like-- </i>
- Gav:<i> Enough of that.</i>

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:07.653 align:start size:88% position:13%
-<i> Let's come back down. </i>
- Dan:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:09.488
Gav:<i> Look at the reflection.
 You see the reflection</i>

00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:12.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
-<i> either side of the spike? </i>
- Dan:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:15.962 align:start size:91% position:9%
-<i> It looks so crystal. </i>
-<i> ( Gav imitating splash )</i>

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.496
 Gav:<i> What are
 we seeing right there?</i>

00:03:17.529 --> 00:03:20.967
Dan:
<i> It looks like a glass sword.</i>

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.370
Gav:<i> That looks amazing.
 Look how smooth that looks.</i>

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:28.708
Gav:<i> Nailed it.</i>

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.376 align:start size:16% position:84%
Nice.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.878 align:start position:0%
Dan, have you ever
done this before?

00:03:32.911 --> 00:03:36.515
What? Sat in a giant wave pool
with a thousand rubber ducks?

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:37.984 align:start size:72% position:28%
