00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:58.371 align:start size:91% position:9%
- It looks like you're
  going off on a voyage. 
- Yeah.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.706
- Looks-- this is fun.
- So how are you gonna

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:02.242 align:start position:0%
get them out of the boat
in the water?

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.511 align:start size:81% position:19%
Oh, I guess really slowly.

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:07.380 align:start position:0%
I'm not really sure
what I'm looking at.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.481 align:start size:44% position:56%
( Dan grunts )

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.621 align:start size:47% position:53%
Bath time.

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:18.758
Gav: That's a lot of ducks.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.031
- Okay, I'm good.
- It looks good.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Done.
- All right, duck close-up.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.535
Dan:<i> I wonder how
 airborne we can get here.</i>

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:32.438
My bet is on, uh, Steven.

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:35.475 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Dan:<i> Oh, yeah, Stevie. </i>
-<i> He's the 95th duck
 from the right.</i>

00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:40.579
Dan:<i> All the ducks are
 in the middle.</i>

00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:43.416
<i> Bwosh! Whoa!</i>

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:50% position:50%
There's one--
one just landed.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.919 align:start size:75% position:25%
One flew off over there.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:49.289
That was amazing.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.959
Dan:<i> It's like
 a really fun bath, this.</i>

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.966
<i> Wow, they flew.
 You nailed the timing there.</i>

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:07.606
Gav:<i> Not the most 
 light up there,</i>

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-<i> but enough to see ducks. </i>
-<i> I mean, you can tell</i>

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.677
<i> what's happening, right?</i>

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.780
It's raining ducks down.

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:17.450 align:start size:91% position:9%
-<i> Those ducks just went-- </i>
- Dan:<i> Bwosh!</i>

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.085
<i> I like how you
 can see the ducks</i>

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.087
<i> on the other side
 of the spike as well.</i>

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.788
<i> If you look at it,
 you look through the water,</i>

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:24.790
<i> you can see through
 mid-air water,</i>

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:26.625
<i> into the base
 of other ducks. </i>

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:28.461
Gav:<i> Yeah. Is that the duck
 that went flying off?</i>

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.662
Dan:<i> I don't know.</i>

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:40.473
Dan:<i> Yeah, I think so.
 Yeah, look there he goes.
 There he goes.</i>

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.108
Gav:<i> One duck
 just sort of flying.</i>

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.809
Dan:<i> He got caught
 the backsplash,</i>

00:05:43.842 --> 00:05:46.479
<i> so he got
 the secondary jet.</i>

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.813
<i> And now
 it's just raining ducks.</i>

